Follow-up fix (post-handoff): the 'exact encode_json for hashref return' assertion was flaky — confirmed empirically that two independently-built Perl hashrefs with identical keys can iterate in different order within the same process (not just across process runs), so encode_json() of two equal-content-but-different-object hashrefs can differ. Fixed by having the test compare against encode_json() of the SAME hashref reference the tool returns, not a freshly-built literal with equal content. Verified with 20x repeated prove runs on t/02 and 10x on the full suite t/ (all green) plus dzil test (Files=8, Tests=86, green).
